We have, $l_{1}=\frac{I \times 2 R}{3 R}=\frac{2 I}{3}\begin{array}{ll}
\therefore & H_{1}=l_{1}^{2} R=\frac{4 l^{2}}{9} \times R...(i) \\
\text{ Also, } & I_{2}=\frac{I \times R}{3 R}=\frac{l}{3} \\
\therefore & H_{2}=I_{2}^{2}(2 R)=\frac{l^{2}}{9} \times 2 R...(ii) \\
\text{ and } & H_{3}=I^{2}(1.5 R)...(iii)
\end{array}
From Eqs. (i), (ii) and (iii), \begin{aligned}$ H_{1}: H_{2}: H_{3} &=$\frac{4 l^{2}}{9} \times$ R: $\frac{I^{2}}{9} \times2 R: I^{2} \times1.5 R \\ \text{ and } =\frac{4}{9}$: $\frac{2}{9}$: 1.5=4: 2: 13.5 \\
&=8: 4: 27
\end{aligned}

Resistance $R=\frac{12 \times 4}{12+4}+2=\frac{48}{16}+2=5 \Omega$ Electric current $I=\frac{E}{R+r}=\frac{12}{6}=2 \mathrm{ A}
\begin{gathered}$ I_{1}+I_{2}=2 $\mathrm{ A}\\
I \propto \frac{1}{R}\\
\therefore \quad I_{2}=1.5 \mathrm{ A},$ I_{1}=0.5 $\mathrm{ A}
\end{gathered}$

$\text{ Given, } \begin{aligned}
\mathrm{R}_{300} &=0.3 \Omega, \mathrm{R}_{\mathrm{t}}=0.6 \Omega, \\
\mathrm{T} &=300 \mathrm{ K}=27^{{}^{\circ}} \mathrm{C}
\end{aligned}$
Temperature coefficient of resistance,
$\alpha=1.5 \times 10^{-3} \mathrm{ K}^{-1}\therefore \quad \quad \mathrm{R}_{300}=\mathrm{R}_{0}(1+\alpha \times 27)\quad 0.3=\mathrm{R}_{0}\left(1+1.5 \times 10^{-3} \times 27\right) \quad \text{...(i)}$ Again, $\quad \mathrm{R}_{\mathrm{t}}=\mathrm{R}_{0}(1+\alpha \mathrm{t})\quad 0.6=\mathrm{R}_{0}\left(1+1.5 \times 10^{-3} \times \mathrm{t}\right) \quad \text{...(ii)}$ Dividing Eq. (ii) by Eq. (i), we get $\quad \frac{0.6}{0.3}=\frac{1+1.5 \times 10^{-3} \mathrm{t}}{1+1.5 \times 10^{-3} \times 27}\Rightarrow \quad 2\left(1+1.5 \times 10^{-3} \times 27\right)=1+1.5 \times 10^{-3} \mathrm{t}\Rightarrow \quad 2+81 \times 10^{-3}=1+1.5 \times 10^{-3} \mathrm{t}\Rightarrow \quad 2+0.081=1+1.5 \times 10^{-3} \mathrm{t}\Rightarrow \quad \mathrm{t}=\frac{1.081}{1.5 \times 10^{-3}}=720^{{}^{\circ}} \mathrm{C}=993 \mathrm{ K}$

Drift velocity, $v_{d}=\frac{1}{n e A} \begin{aligned}
\Rightarrow$ v_{d} &=$\frac{5}{\left(5 \times 10^{26}\right) \times\left(1.6 \times 10^{-19}\right) \times\left(4 \times 10^{-6}\right)}$\\
&=$\frac{1}{64}=1.56 \times10^{-2} \mathrm{ ms}^{-1}
\end{aligned}$
